    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d217">

                <pb facs="0389" n="301" xml:id="pg301"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119 P 43/910: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Special
                        Representative</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">House</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-19T16:00:00-05:00"
                            >November 19, 1918—4 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>50. [From President Wilson.] Referring to your 119,<anchor n="11"
                        xml:id="d217-f1"/> shall try to get Miss Tarbell to go over.</p>
                <p>Referring to your 120,<anchor n="12" xml:id="d217-f2"/> I entirely approve, and
                    hope that you will in my name urge the acquiescence of the Supreme Command. This
                    seems to me essential to a peaceful settlement. Woodrow Wilson.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
